  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "So, I noticed that converting Dynamic Bones to Phys Bones will not really use the last bone in the chain, it will not be rotated or anything else, it will basically be ignored by Phys Bones. I know that the docs state that a chain with a single root bone and with several children (but no grandchildren) will require to manually add an endpoint. But this basically seems to apply to every Phys Bone, since if you had a chain out of 2 bones, the last bone will not be used unless you manually set an endpoint for it compared to Dynamic Bones. This basically means that every Phys Bone will always miss the last bone in the chain compared to Dynamic Bones.\nI know that we can manually add endpoints to all of our bones, but why is this now always required? This does not only make it harder to manually convert to Phys Bones in your own Unity project, but will also break a lot of Avatars that can only be converted in game by the auto conversion (SDK2 Avatars and also Public Avatars that you might not have access to)\nIf Phys Bones would handle the end of a chain the same way as Dynamic Bones, did it would solve a lot of problems, auto conversion would work better, chains with a single root bone and with several children (but no grandchildren) would work out of the box, converting them manually in Unity would also work better since you wouldn’t need to always add an endpoint and in general it would just make it easier for everyone. Please consider changing it.\nIn the video I included below you can see what I mean, the whiskers will not move in the middle without manually adding an end point compared to Dynamic Bones.\nhttps://youtu.be/oKkCS8KzNqg\nIn the first picture you can see how it normally should look like with both bones being used on the whiskers, this requires manually adding end points though. In the second picture you can see how it worked with the auto conversion, it completely misses the end of the bones.",
